From ef3e17f81f512a655ba40e64f1d4eda09ef50d54 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:26:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GX front end: a draw's transform state copied only when its
 version changed

Every draw's 2.3 KB of transform state (matrices, lights, the XF register
window) was copied three times on the GX worker: from the parser's state into
the draw queue, from the queue into the packet, from the packet into the
sink's draw. About 95 percent of draws repeat the draw before's transform
(a model's shapes share its matrices), and the transform version (0127) says
when: the same nonzero version, the same state. Now the queue slot of such a
draw keeps only its own fields and names the slot with the arrays (source),
the packet keeps its arrays when they are that version's, and the sink's
retained draw keeps its own. DOL_GX_TRANSFORM_VERIFY=1 copies every time and
counts any difference from what would have been kept ([gx-transform] lines).

Checked on the i9 + RTX 5090 (BlueWake, the 2026-10-02 module):
- The verify mode over twelve places by warp (Outset, Dragon Roost Island and
  Cavern, Forest Haven, the sea, the Forbidden Woods, the Tower of the Gods,
  the Forsaken Fortress, Hyrule, Hyrule Castle, the Earth Temple's boss, the
  Wind Temple): 54 million draws, 95 percent kept, 0 differences.
- Synchronous captures against the build before: the Outset route 19 of 19,
  Gohma's room 26 of 26 identical, Link's position the same at every probe;
  Smooth Motion dumps of Gohma's room (game frames 300-330) 62 of 62.
- Four E-cores, uncapped, Smooth Motion off, the heaviest places of a warp
  survey, two runs each: the GX worker's CPU per game frame at Forest Haven
  25.5-26.3 ms before, 22.3-22.7 after; Hyrule Castle's room 22.0-22.4 and
  19.0-20.6; Dragon Roost Island 20.4-21.6 and 18.5-18.8; Hyrule 18.1-19.3 and
  15.2-15.5; the sea by the Forsaken Fortress 16.6-18.2 and 14.8-15.4; game
  frames a second up 6 to 16 percent there.
